Display off switches the WLED module off (MOD_EN), not only its brightness to 0; black frame when it cannot.
User report (boot 1136): when the screen times out the last frame stays visible, "with the backlight off". 0242's
blSet(false) wrote 0 to the two WLED4 sink brightness registers and left WLED_CTRL MOD_EN (0xd846 bit 7) set.
qcom-wled never does that: WLED4's floor is 0.4 % (wled4_set_brightness), and a brightness of 0 is
wled_module_enable(0). Now:
 - sweet_spmi.c: sweet_spmi_wled_module(on), MOD_EN bit 7 only (read-modify-write, read back); 0xd846 is accepted
   by the write whitelist only during that function's own write. Write channels 6 -> 8 (6 in use with
   sweetcharger=2).
 - SweetFramebuffer: display off = brightness 0, then the module off; display on = brightness back, then the module
   on (qcom-wled's order), retried like the brightness. If the module could not be switched off (or with
   sweetfb_blmod=0) the panel gets the black frame of the old fallback; display on redraws the latest frame first.

